readBrace accepts a ${...} body only in these shapes:
- an optional leading # (length);
- a name: an identifier, positional digits, or one of the special parameters @ * # ? $ ! -;
- optionally one operator from :- - :+ + :? ? # ## % %%;
- after the operator, a word that holds no $( ${ $[ backquote, quote, <( or >(. A plain $name inside the word stays allowed.

Every other body is undecidable. That covers indirection (${!x}), transformations (${x@P}), assignment (${x=...}, ${x:=...}), substring offsets (${x:off}, which are arithmetic), replacement and case operators (${x/a/b}, ${x^^}), and anything the shapes above do not match. The reviewer's process-substitution probes and planted-value probes become table cases, and the plain-usage set stays allowed.

